<!-- HEADER -->
<header>
  <div class="header-inner">
    <div class="report-label">Market Intelligence Report · Q1 2026</div>
    <h1>Global Smartwatch Secondary Market Analysis</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Pricing dynamics, geographic arbitrage, and seller behavior across 3,607 resale listings — Apple, Garmin, and Samsung.</p>
    <div class="meta">
      <div class="meta-item"><div class="meta-label">Total Listings</div><div class="meta-value">3,607</div></div>
      <div class="meta-item"><div class="meta-label">Unique Sellers</div><div class="meta-value">1,754</div></div>
      <div class="meta-item"><div class="meta-label">Countries</div><div class="meta-value">20+</div></div>
      <div class="meta-item"><div class="meta-label">Price Floor</div><div class="meta-value">$70 USD</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- NAV -->
<nav>
  <div class="nav-inner">
    <a href="#overview">Market Overview</a>
    <a href="#brand-pricing">Brand Pricing</a>
    <a href="#geo">Geographic Arbitrage</a>
    <a href="#case-size">Case Size Premium</a>
    <a href="#sellers">Power Sellers</a>
    <a href="#recommendations">Recommendations</a>
  </div>
</nav>

<div class="container">

<!-- ===================== SECTION 1: MARKET OVERVIEW ===================== -->
<section id="overview">
  <div class="section-number">Section 01</div>
  <h2>Market Overview &amp; Listing Composition</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">3,607 active secondary-market listings collected in Q1 2026 across Apple, Garmin, and Samsung. Apple dominates supply; the US is the primary marketplace with 2,344 listings.</p>

  <div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi-card"><div class="kpi-label">Total Listings</div><div class="kpi-value">3,607</div><div class="kpi-sub">Above $70 USD price floor</div></div>
    <div class="kpi-card"><div class="kpi-label">Unique Sellers</div><div class="kpi-value">1,754</div><div class="kpi-sub">Avg 2.06 listings/seller</div></div>
    <div class="kpi-card"><div class="kpi-label">Brands Covered</div><div class="kpi-value">3</div><div class="kpi-sub">Apple, Garmin, Samsung</div></div>
    <div class="kpi-card"><div class="kpi-label">Worldwide Shipping</div><div class="kpi-value">27.3%</div><div class="kpi-sub">986 of 3,607 listings</div></div>
    <div class="kpi-card"><div class="kpi-label">New Condition</div><div class="kpi-value">43.1%</div><div class="kpi-sub">1,553 listings</div></div>
    <div class="kpi-card"><div class="kpi-label">Used Condition</div><div class="kpi-value">34.7%</div><div class="kpi-sub">1,250 listings</div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="two-col">
    <div class="chart-wrap">
      <div class="chart-title">Brand Distribution</div>
      <div class="chart-note">Share of total listings</div>
      <div class="chart-canvas-wrap" style="height:220px;">
        <canvas id="brandDistChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-wrap">
      <div class="chart-title">Condition Mix</div>
      <div class="chart-note">All listing conditions (primary categories)</div>
      <div class="chart-canvas-wrap" style="height:220px;">
        <canvas id="conditionChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-wrap">
    <div class="chart-title">Top 10 Countries by Listing Volume</div>
    <div class="chart-note">Number of listings per country</div>
    <canvas id="countryChart" style="max-height:260px;"></canvas>
  </div>

</section>

<!-- ===================== SECTION 2: BRAND PRICING ===================== -->
<section id="brand-pricing">
  <div class="section-number">Section 02</div>
  <h2>Brand-Level Pricing &amp; Value Retention</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">Garmin commands the highest median resale price ($567), followed by Apple ($550) and Samsung ($530). Apple carries the widest price variance — driven by premium Hermès editions and bundles that push the ceiling to $40,500.</p>

  <div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi-card" style="border-color:#2563eb55;">
      <div class="kpi-label" style="color:#60a5fa;">Apple Median</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">$550</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Range: $120 – $40,500</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card" style="border-color:#16a34a55;">
      <div class="kpi-label" style="color:#4ade80;">Garmin Median</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">$567</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Range: $215 – $1,319</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card" style="border-color:#dc262655;">
      <div class="kpi-label" style="color:#f87171;">Samsung Median</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">$530</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Range: $245 – $49,900</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-label">Apple Condition Premium</div>
      <div class="kpi-value" style="color:var(--positive);">+17.7%</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">New vs. Used median price</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-label">Garmin Condition Premium</div>
      <div class="kpi-value" style="color:var(--muted);">−0.3%</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Effectively no premium</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-label">Samsung Condition Premium</div>
      <div class="kpi-value" style="color:var(--muted);">+0.6%</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Minimal premium</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="two-col">
    <div class="chart-wrap">
      <div class="chart-title">Median Listing Price by Brand</div>
      <div class="chart-note">USD — primary value retention benchmark</div>
      <canvas id="brandMedianChart" style="max-height:220px;"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-wrap">
      <div class="chart-title">Mean Price by Brand</div>
      <div class="chart-note">USD — inflated by outliers, especially Apple &amp; Samsung</div>
      <canvas id="brandMeanChart" style="max-height:220px;"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-wrap">
    <div class="chart-title">New vs. Used Median Price by Brand</div>
    <div class="chart-note">Only "New" and "Used" condition listings included</div>
    <canvas id="newUsedChart" style="max-height:260px;"></canvas>
  </div>

  <div class="callout">
    <div class="callout-title">Key Insight — Condition Premium</div>
    <p>Apple is the only brand where condition meaningfully affects resale price: New Apple watches command a <strong>17.7% premium</strong> ($589 vs $501 median). Garmin and Samsung show near-zero condition premium, suggesting the resale buyer base treats condition as irrelevant for those brands — or that secondary-market listings don't reliably differentiate genuine "new" stock.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Brand</th><th>Listings</th><th>Median Price</th><th>Mean Price</th><th>Std Dev</th><th>Min</th><th>Max</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="brand-apple">Apple</td><td>2,370</td><td>$550.00</td><td>$594.55</td><td>$834.18</td><td>$120.00</td><td>$40,500.00</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="brand-garmin">Garmin</td><td>746</td><td>$566.98</td><td>$628.05</td><td>$198.00</td><td>$215.10</td><td>$1,319.00</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="brand-samsung">Samsung</td><td>470</td><td>$530.00</td><td>$725.49</td><td>$2,285.92</td><td>$244.99</td><td>$49,900.00</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="callout" style="background: rgba(220,38,38,0.06); border-color: rgba(220,38,38,0.3);">
    <div class="callout-title" style="color:#f87171;">Outlier Alert — Samsung &amp; Apple</div>
    <p>Samsung's mean price ($725) is $195 above its median ($530), inflated by extreme outliers reaching $49,900. Apple's max of $40,500 similarly skews the mean. When making inventory decisions, <strong>use median price</strong> as the operative benchmark — the mean is unreliable for these brands.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== SECTION 3: GEOGRAPHIC ARBITRAGE ===================== -->
<section id="geo">
  <div class="section-number">Section 03</div>
  <h2>Geographic Pricing Arbitrage</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">Significant cross-border price gaps exist for all three brands. The UK underprices Apple by 28.6%; Canada overprices Garmin by 57%; and the UK commands a 55.7% premium for Samsung — creating concrete sourcing and resale arbitrage windows.</p>

  <div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi-card" style="border-color:#2563eb55;">
      <div class="kpi-label" style="color:#60a5fa;">Apple Price Spread</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">$399</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">UK ($393) ↔ Australia ($792)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card" style="border-color:#16a34a55;">
      <div class="kpi-label" style="color:#4ade80;">Garmin Price Spread</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">$384</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Japan ($506) ↔ Canada ($890)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card" style="border-color:#dc262655;">
      <div class="kpi-label" style="color:#f87171;">Samsung Price Spread</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">$388</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Japan ($437) ↔ UK ($825)</div>
    </div>
